<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to May 2.</p>
<p>    Top 10 gains in year Price  percent</p>
<p>Rank Name		    May 2  change</p>
<p> 1  Sthn Pac Pete	  3.84  222.69</p>
<p> 2  Oil Search	     3.05  142.06</p>
<p> 3  Natl Aust Bank	17.70   55.13</p>
<p> 4  Howard Smith	  11.35   51.74</p>
<p> 5  CSL Limited	    7.15   48.34</p>
<p> 6  Transurban Group   900.00   41.18</p>
<p> 7  Leighton Hlds	  5.77   40.73</p>
<p> 8  Woodside Petrolm    10.30   38.81</p>
<p> 9  Amalgamated Hlds     7.00   38.61</p>
<p>10  Flc-Energy Div	 3.72   38.29</p>
<p>Top 10 falls in year    Price  percent</p>
<p>Rank Name		    May 2  change</p>
<p> 1  Acacia Resources     1.80  -45.29</p>
<p> 2  Newcrest Mining	3.45  -44.35</p>
<p> 3  Goldfields	     2.02  -38.79</p>
<p> 4  Sons Of Gwalia	 5.58  -38.00</p>
<p> 5  Great Central	  2.49  -37.75</p>
<p> 6  Plutonic Rsc	   4.90  -36.53</p>
<p> 7  Davids Limited	 1.30  -29.73</p>
<p> 8  RGC			4.70  -29.64</p>
<p> 9  Normandy Min	   1.60  -27.93</p>
<p>10  News Corp-Prefd	4.84  -25.54</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
